{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And lest you lift up your eyes.</b> To gaze at the thing and to set the heart to stray after them." "<b>Which YHWH allotted.</b> To illuminate for them (Megillah 9); another interpretation — for divinities: He did not withhold them from straying after them, but rather allotted them with words of their futility, to drive them from the world. And so it says (Psalms 36): ״כִּי הֶחֱלִיק אֵלָיו בְּעֵינָיו לִמְצֹא עֲוֹנוֹ לִשְׂנֹא״ (Avodah Zarah 55)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:59.095805582Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}